Subject: [P20 review] winedmo retain native decoder coordinates and parser drain

Residual against GE-Proton11-9 after ge-video-rework.
Source-reviewed only: not compiler or runtime qualification.
Prior P19b2 patch ownership (some behavior is now upstream):
  ge-master-20260913-se2-p8/0047-winedmo-expose-ac3-and-eac3-audio-decoding.patch
  ge-proton11-6/0008-winedmo-preserve-audio-timeline-across-flush.patch
  ge-proton11-7-se2-p19b/0070-winedmo-preserve-decoder-demux-coordinate.patch
  proposed/0037-winedmo-discard-resampler-delay-on-flush.patch
  proposed/0048-winedmo-expose-existing-dts-alac-and-g711-decoders.patch
  proposed/0053-winedmo-map-exact-h264-es-subtype.patch
  proposed/0054-winedmo-drain-parser-tail-before-decoder-eos.patch
  proposed/0056-winedmo-preserve-vc1-input-timestamp-origin.patch
  proposed/0062-winedmo-use-zero-based-parser-byte-position.patch
Rebased onto GE-Proton11-11 (SE3-P1)

